// =====================================================================
// SCENE 6 · GAP 3: HINTS FOR THE FRIENDS (00:00)
// Fal lived. Night Anin stops targeting him and turns to Anin's
// friends, so they start to see the loop.
//
// NOTES FOR THE PROGRAMMER
// - Every "//" comment is a stage direction for you, not in-game text.
// - FROM THIS SCENE ON, night Anin's lines use the speaker "Night Anin"
//   (different name tag / text colour). Before this scene she was
//   plain "Anin" on purpose, to hide the twist.
// - Same sprite as day Anin. No visual difference.
// - Same gap rules: no NPCs, clocks frozen at 00:00, gap colour grade.
// - Commands used (new ones marked NEW):
//     <<gap_mode true/false>>, <<quest_start>>, <<quest_update>>,
//     <<scene_transition>>, <<end_gap>>  (same as before)
//     <<edit_calendar>>     NEW  every December date becomes "10";
//                                the circled 12th stays untouched
//     <<draw_sketchbook>>   NEW  drawing animation, NOT blurred
// - Speaker "Note" = text shown on screen in Anin's handwriting.
// - Order (linear, no fail state): calendar -> Dira's book (classroom)
//   -> Lila's sketchbook (locker room) -> back to dorm.
// - World state for Day 4: calendar all 10s, margin note in Dira's
//   book, Lila's sketchbook full of Warmus lunches.
// =====================================================================


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — 00:00
// Interactables: Gap3_KiranaBed, Gap3_Calendar, Gap3_Door
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap3_Start
tags: scene6 gap3 dorm
---
<<advance_time "dream">>
<<gap_mode true>>
// Lets the Dorm door run Gap3_Door instead of leaving freely.
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<set $gap3_calendar to false>>
<<set $gap3_dira to false>>
<<set $gap3_lila to false>>
Night Anin: He lived.
Night Anin: She learned how to save him. Of course she did. So did I, once.
Night Anin: Killing him only teaches her to save him. Fine.
Night Anin: If she won't let go for him, maybe she'll let go for them.
<<quest_start "gap3" "Make them see it">>
===

title: Gap3_KiranaBed
tags: scene6 gap3 dorm interactable
---
Night Anin: Empty. Like always, in here.
===

title: Gap3_Calendar
tags: scene6 gap3 dorm interactable required
---
// Kirana's calendar.
<<if $gap3_calendar is false>>
    Night Anin: December. One day circled. The twelfth. "Ferry, 06:00."
    Night Anin: She's leaving. She never told us.
    <<edit_calendar>>
    Night Anin: Every day is the tenth. Let her see it.
    <<set $gap3_calendar to true>>
    <<quest_update "gap3" "Go to the classroom">>
<<else>>
    Night Anin: Every day is the tenth.
<<endif>>
===

title: Gap3_Door
tags: scene6 gap3 dorm interactable
---
<<if $gap3_calendar is false>>
    Night Anin: Not yet.
<<elseif $gap3_lila is false>>
    <<scene_transition "LockerRoom">>
<<else>>
    <<jump Gap3_Dorm_End>>
<<endif>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// CLASSROOM — 00:00
// Interactable: Gap3_DiraBook (Dira's desk, book left open)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap3_DiraBook
tags: scene6 gap3 classroom interactable required
---
<<if $gap3_dira is false>>
    Night Anin: She always reads the same page. Every morning, the same page.
    Night Anin: She told us she already knows what's written there. She does.
    // Underline a line on the page and write in the margin.
    Note: "You've read this before."
    <<set $gap3_dira to true>>
    <<quest_update "gap3" "Go to the locker room">>
<<else>>
    Night Anin: She'll know the handwriting.
<<endif>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// LOCKER ROOM — 00:00
// Interactables: Gap3_LilaLocker, Gap3_LilaSketchbook
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap3_LilaLocker
tags: scene6 gap3 lockers interactable
---
Night Anin: She leaves her sketchbook here every night. Every single night.
===

title: Gap3_LilaSketchbook
tags: scene6 gap3 lockers interactable required
---
<<if $gap3_dira is false>>
    Night Anin: Dira first.
<<elseif $gap3_lila is false>>
    Night Anin: The drawing of the four of them. Still not finished.
    Night Anin: She'll never finish it. Not here.
    // No blur this time. Night Anin hides nothing anymore.
    <<draw_sketchbook>>
    Night Anin: Lunch at Warmus. The four of them. Same table, same food. Again. And again. And again.
    <<set $gap3_lila to true>>
    <<quest_update "gap3" "Go back to the dorm">>
    // Same as Gap 1: back to the Dorm, where Gap3_Dorm_End is the start
    // node while $gap3_lila is true.
    <<scene_transition "Dorm">>
<<else>>
    Night Anin: Again. And again.
<<endif>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — 00:00 (END)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap3_Dorm_End
tags: scene6 gap3 dorm
---
Night Anin: She's lost count of how many times she's watched him die.
Night Anin: I stopped counting long before she did.
Night Anin: I don't even remember what Dira's laugh sounds like anymore.
// The second hand moves.
<<gap_mode false>>
<<set $chapter_scene to 7>>
<<end_gap>>
// TRANSITION → Scene 7: Day 4
===
